.TH mnnn-peers 1  "mnnn-peers 2.20.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-peers \- Your peers and what each has for you (shares, live sessions, executables, sites); run a peer\*(Aqs executable or ask it for something
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn peers\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Your peers and what each has for you (shares, live sessions, executables, sites); run a peer\*(Aqs executable or ask it for something
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<stream|poll>\fR
How live collaboration reaches peers: `stream` (gRPC streams, the default) or `poll` (requests over the peer connection; for containers). Overrides MUNINN_COLLAB_TRANSPORT and the `net config \-\-collab\-transport` setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Live collaboration works between nodes that exchanged keys (connections, linked nodes, org members). Messages are kept on both sides and retried by the running node until delivered. A live session is hosted by the node that has the item; invited peers join, edit and see each other's cursors, and every edit is merged without loss and written back to the item. `mnnn peers show PEER` lists what a peer offers you; `mnnn peers run` calls an org executable on it with your role's permissions. `mnnn help collaboration` has the guide.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-peers\-show(1)
What a peer has for you: shared items, live sessions, executables and sites
.TP
mnnn\-peers\-run(1)
Run one of a peer\*(Aqs org executables (an endpoint); results stream as they arrive
.TP
mnnn\-peers\-request(1)
Ask a peer for something (a share, an invitation, access): sends a message
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
